.TH X11SHIFT 1 "October 2026" "X11Shift 1.1.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
x11shift \- graphical color temperature control for X11 desktops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B x11shift
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B X11Shift
is a GTK application that changes the gamma ramps of active X11 displays
through XRandR. The graphical settings window controls color temperature,
brightness, schedule, transition duration, location, and selected displays.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start hidden in the desktop notification area. This is used by autostart.
.TP
.B --reset
Set the gamma ramps and native color lookup tables of active displays to
linear and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/x11shift/config.ini
Per-user settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/x11shift.desktop
Created or removed by the autostart checkbox.
.SH NOTES
X11Shift requires an X11 session and XRandR 1.3 or newer. Some proprietary
graphics drivers do not expose writable gamma ramps. Wayland sessions are not
supported by this version.
.PP
If sunrise-to-sunset scheduling is selected without a configured location,
X11Shift uses the custom day and night times until latitude or longitude is
entered.
.PP
The notification icon uses the legacy GTK tray protocol. If the desktop does
not provide a compatible notification area, launch X11Shift again to reopen its
existing settings window.
.PP
On drivers exposing a native GAMMA_LUT output property, X11Shift uses that
property to commit color changes to the GPU. This handles AMD Xorg sessions
where legacy gamma requests update cached ramps without changing the display.
Disabling adjustment or quitting restores the original lookup table.
.PP
Original native lookup tables are retained in the X11 session so a restarted
process can recover from its own leftover tint instead of treating night colors
as the original calibration. Recovery also applies when adjustment is disabled
at startup.
